Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: pam-gnupg
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, gnupg (>= 2.1)
Description: PAM module to unlock GnuPG keys at login (upstream source build)
 pam-gnupg presets the GnuPG agent's passphrase cache using the login
 password, so a user's GnuPG key (and anything backed by it, such as a
 pass(1) password store) is unlocked automatically at login instead of
 prompting separately.
 .
 This package builds upstream's autotools source (v0.4) rather than
 repackaging a binary, since pam-gnupg ships no pre-built releases.
 .
 System-level PAM stack wiring (/etc/pam.d/*) is handled by
 paperweight-secrets, not by this package.
